  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Sorting Visualizer \u2014 Quicksort in Real Time\n\n**Sorting** is one of the most fundamental problems in computer science. Comparison-based sorting algorithms \u2014 those that determine order purely by comparing elements \u2014 have a well-known information-theoretic lower bound:\n\n$$\\Omega(n \\log n)$$\n\nAny algorithm that sorts $n$ elements by comparison alone must make at least $\\log_2(n!)\\approx n\\log_2 n$ comparisons in the worst case.\n\n## Quicksort\n\n**Quicksort** is a divide-and-conquer algorithm invented by Tony Hoare in 1959. Its strategy:\n\n1. **Choose a pivot** element from the array.\n2. **Partition** the array so all elements less than the pivot come before it and all greater elements come after it.\n3. **Recurse** on the two sub-arrays.\n\n### Complexity\n\n| Case    | Time         | Space     |\n|---------|--------------|----------|\n| Average | $O(n \\log n)$ | $O(\\log n)$ |\n| Worst   | $O(n^2)$      | $O(n)$    |\n\nThe worst case occurs when the pivot consistently lands at one extreme (e.g., always picking the smallest or largest element on an already-sorted array). Good pivot selection \u2014 randomization or median-of-three \u2014 makes the worst case extremely unlikely.\n\n## This Visualization\n\nWe sort an array of **100 bars** whose heights represent values 1\u2013100. The simulation runs step-by-step at ~30 FPS, coloring bars to show:\n\n- 🟦 **Steel blue**: unprocessed bars\n- 🟡 **Yellow**: currently being compared\n- 🔴 **Red**: the pivot element\n- 🟢 **Green**: confirmed in their final sorted position\n\nA live statistics panel tracks the comparison and swap counts in real time.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Quicksort Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Quicksort \u2014 incremental step-by-step simulation using the Simulation trait.\n//\n// Because tick() must be incremental (one call per frame), we drive quicksort\n// via an explicit stack of pending partition ranges rather than recursion.\n// Each tick performs a few comparison/swap steps and publishes live stats.\n\nconst N: usize = 100;\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst STEPS_PER_TICK: usize = 4;\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\nenum Phase {\n    Idle,\n    Partitioning { lo: usize, hi: usize, pivot_val: u32, store: usize, k: usize },\n    Done,\n}\n\nstruct SortVis {\n    arr: Vec<u32>,\n    stack: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n    phase: Phase,\n    comparisons: u64,\n    swaps: u64,\n    sorted: bool,\n    comparing: Option<(usize, usize)>,\n    pivot_highlight: Option<usize>,\n    sorted_indices: Vec<bool>,\n    sweep: usize,\n}\n\nimpl SortVis {\n    // Lomuto partition scheme, driven one step at a time.\n    // Returns Some(pivot_final_index) when the partition is complete.\n    fn partition_step(&mut self, lo: usize, hi: usize, pivot_val: u32, store: usize, k: usize) -> Option<usize> {\n        if k <= hi {\n            self.comparisons += 1;\n            self.comparing = Some((k, hi));\n            if self.arr[k] <= pivot_val {\n                self.arr.swap(store, k);\n                self.swaps += 1;\n                self.phase = Phase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store: store + 1, k: k + 1 };\n            } else {\n                self.phase = Phase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store, k: k + 1 };\n            }\n            None\n        } else {\n            // Place the pivot (currently at hi) into its final slot.\n            // During Lomuto we moved the pivot to hi before we started, so swap store \u2194 hi.\n            self.arr.swap(store, hi);\n            self.swaps += 1;\n            self.comparing = None;\n            Some(store)\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Simulation for SortVis {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        let mut arr: Vec<u32> = (1..=N as u32).collect();\n\n        // Deterministic Fisher-Yates shuffle via LCG PRNG.\n        let mut seed: u64 = 42;\n        for i in (1..N).rev() {\n            seed = seed.wrapping_mul(6_364_136_223_846_793_005).wrapping_add(1);\n            let j = (seed >> 33) as usize % (i + 1);\n            arr.swap(i, j);\n        }\n\n        // Lomuto requires the pivot to be at the right end of the range.\n        // We push the initial range and let Idle do the setup.\n        let mut stack = Vec::new();\n        stack.push((0, N - 1));\n\n        Self {\n            arr,\n            stack,\n            phase: Phase::Idle,\n            comparisons: 0,\n            swaps: 0,\n            sorted: false,\n            comparing: None,\n            pivot_highlight: None,\n            sorted_indices: vec![false; N],\n            sweep: 0,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        // Run STEPS_PER_TICK incremental steps of the sort state machine.\n        for _ in 0..STEPS_PER_TICK {\n            match self.phase {\n                Phase::Done => {}\n                Phase::Idle => {\n                    match self.stack.pop() {\n                        None => {\n                            self.sorted = true;\n                            self.phase = Phase::Done;\n                        }\n                        Some((lo, hi)) => {\n                            if lo >= hi {\n                                // Single-element range is already sorted.\n                                self.sorted_indices[lo] = true;\n                                // Stay in Idle to pop the next range.\n                            } else {\n                                // Lomuto: move pivot (arr[hi]) aside \u2014 it\u2019s already at hi.\n                                let pivot_val = self.arr[hi];\n                                self.pivot_highlight = Some(hi);\n                                self.phase = Phase::Partitioning {\n                                    lo,\n                                    hi,\n                                    pivot_val,\n                                    store: lo,\n                                    k: lo,\n                                };\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                Phase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store, k } => {\n                    if let Some(pivot_pos) = self.partition_step(lo, hi, pivot_val, store, k) {\n                        self.sorted_indices[pivot_pos] = true;\n                        self.pivot_highlight = None;\n                        // Push sub-ranges (avoid underflow on lo).\n                        if pivot_pos > lo {\n                            self.stack.push((lo, pivot_pos - 1));\n                        } else {\n                            if lo < N { self.sorted_indices[lo] = true; }\n                        }\n                        if pivot_pos + 1 <= hi {\n                            self.stack.push((pivot_pos + 1, hi));\n                        } else {\n                            if hi < N { self.sorted_indices[hi] = true; }\n                        }\n                        self.phase = Phase::Idle;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // When done, run a sweep to paint all bars green over several ticks.\n        if self.sorted && self.sweep < N {\n            let end = (self.sweep + 5).min(N);\n            for i in self.sweep..end {\n                self.sorted_indices[i] = true;\n            }\n            self.sweep = end;\n        }\n\n        // Publish stats for the LiveView cell.\n        sim::publish(\"comparisons\", &self.comparisons);\n        sim::publish(\"swaps\", &self.swaps);\n        sim::publish(\"sorted\", &self.sorted);\n\n        // \u2500\u2500 Render \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n        let bar_w = W / N as u32;\n        let mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\n        canvas.fill((26, 26, 46)); // #1a1a2e\n\n        let comparing_pair = self.comparing;\n        let pivot_idx = self.pivot_highlight;\n\n        for i in 0..N {\n            let val = self.arr[i];\n            let bar_h = (val as u32 * (H - 4)) / N as u32;\n            let x0 = i as u32 * bar_w;\n            let y0 = H - bar_h;\n\n            let color = if self.sorted_indices[i] {\n                (68, 204, 68)   // green  #44CC44\n            } else if Some(i) == pivot_idx {\n                (255, 68, 68)   // red    #FF4444\n            } else if comparing_pair.map_or(false, |(a, b)| i == a || i == b) {\n                (255, 215, 0)   // yellow #FFD700\n            } else {\n                (70, 130, 180)  // steel blue #4682B4\n            };\n\n            for x in x0..x0 + bar_w.saturating_sub(1) {\n                for y in y0..H {\n                    canvas.set_pixel(x, y, color);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        canvas\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        30\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Statistics",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Live statistics dashboard reading published values from the simulation cell.\n\nstruct Stats {\n    tick: u32,\n}\n\nimpl LiveView for Stats {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { tick: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        self.tick += 1;\n        let comps = sim::read::<u64>(\"comparisons\").unwrap_or(0);\n        let swaps = sim::read::<u64>(\"swaps\").unwrap_or(0);\n        let done = sim::read::<bool>(\"sorted\").unwrap_or(false);\n\n        let status = if done { \"\u2705 SORTED\" } else { \"\u23f3 SORTING...\" };\n        let color = if done { \"#44cc44\" } else { \"#ffd700\" };\n\n        LiveContent::Html(format!(r#\"<div style=\"font-family: monospace; background: #1a1a2e; color: #e0e0e0; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; display: flex; gap: 32px; align-items: center;\">\n            <div><span style=\"color: #888;\">Comparisons:</span> <span style=\"color: #4fc3f7; font-size: 1.3em;\">{comps}</span></div>\n            <div><span style=\"color: #888;\">Swaps:</span> <span style=\"color: #ff6b6b; font-size: 1.3em;\">{swaps}</span></div>\n            <div><span style=\"color: {color}; font-size: 1.3em; font-weight: bold;\">{status}</span></div>\n        </div>\"#))\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        5\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ]
}
